    {
      "id": "proj0004",
      "title": {
        "es": "Andrés Irasuste Psicología Hoy",
        "en": "Psicoterapia Hoy",
        "esAuto": false
      },
      "subtitle": {
        "es": "Andrés Irasuste Psicólogo",
        "en": "Andrés Irasuste Psicólogo",
        "esAuto": true
      },
      "role": {
        "es": "",
        "en": "",
        "esAuto": true
      },
      "year": "2019",
      "theme": "dark",
      "tags": {
        "category": [],
        "industry": []
      },
      "token": {
        "image": "projects/proj0004/icons_12.svg",
        "width": 68,
        "x": 0.425,
        "y": 0.479,
        "rotation": 0,
        "hoverFx": "none",
        "inkColor": "#000000",
        "float": true,
        "watercolor": {
          "on": true,
          "colors": [
            "#ff5221",
            "#ff5221",
            "#ff5221"
          ],
          "blend": "normal",
          "layer": "under"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "variant": "body",
          "content": {
            "es": "Dar el primer paso en salud mental suele estar acompañado de dudas, indecisión y postergación. Con esto en mente, creamos el concepto \"Hoy\" para la marca del psicólogo Andrés Irasuste: un llamado a la acción que busca transformar la duda en decisión.\n\nDiseñamos el logotipo y piezas gráficas para redes sociales enfocados en transmitir cercanía, priorizando el bienestar presente sin dejarlo para después.",
            "en": "Taking the first step in mental health care is often met with hesitation, self-doubt, and procrastination. With this in mind, we built the brand concept \"Hoy\" (Today) for psychologist Andrés Irasuste—a call to action designed to transform uncertainty into action.\n\nWe crafted the logo and social media design system to feel approachable and reassuring, encouraging people to prioritize their well-being now rather than putting it off.\n",
            "esAuto": false
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "row",
          "columns": 3,
          "cells": [
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "projects/proj0004/Asset-1.webp",
